1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
NiyamSetu turns admission uploads into traceable, policy-aware records.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
An institution uploads the standard CSV and receives an immutable receipt.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Every row is explained: accepted, invalid, or sent for accountable human review.

4
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Staff can find a student record without copying long internal identifiers.

5
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The decision keeps its ruleset, approval source, findings, and governed history.

6
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Evidence can be exported with section checksums and a Merkle root for tamper detection.

7
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Corrections and cancellations follow a visible reviewer and checker workflow.

8
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Policy Lab separates the source-aligned baseline from an unapproved proposal.

9
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Each changed outcome is tied to a real rule code. The simulation never writes to the live ledger.

10
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Role boundaries are enforced. A reviewer cannot use the verifier-only workflow.

11
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:06,000
An authorized verifier receives only the claims allowed by purpose, scope, and expiry.

12
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The local receipt is Ed25519-signed and refreshable. Official APAAR integration remains intentionally unclaimed.
